course: dictionary
lesson: 7108
title: Pebbles and how they get smooth
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A pebble is a small, smooth, round stone, often found on beaches and in rivers. Read the words around it to understand it: «Curiosity found smooth, rounded pebbles like those in a stream, a sign that water once flowed there.» Smooth and rounded tell you what a pebble looks like, and a stream is where you might find one.
explain: Why are pebbles round? Water rubs them for a long time. In science this is called erosion: moving water and waves wear rough rocks down into smooth stones. Think of a rough rock in a river slowly rubbed into a pebble over many years.
explain: The word pebble can also be a clue to size. «Asteroids are... lumps of rock and metal from pebble size up to hundreds of kilometres across.» So pebble size means small, like a stone you could hold in your hand. Swap in your meaning to check it still makes sense.
fact: A pebble is a small, smooth, round stone.
fact: Pebbles are often found on beaches and in rivers.
fact: Pebbles are rounded because water rubbed them for a long time.
fact: Erosion is when moving water and waves wear rough rocks into smooth stones.
fact: A «pebble beach» is a beach covered in pebbles instead of sand.
exercise: «Curiosity found smooth, rounded pebbles like those in a stream.» What is a pebble? | A large, sharp rock on a mountain | A type of sand | *A small, smooth, round stone | A kind of seaweed
exercise: Why are pebbles round and smooth? | They were cut by people with tools | They grow into a round shape on trees | They are made of soft paper | *Water rubbed them for a long time
exercise: «Asian small-clawed otters... juggle pebbles with their paws.» What do the otters juggle? | Leaves | Fish | Sticks | *Pebbles
test: «Asteroids are... lumps of rock and metal from pebble size up to hundreds of kilometres across.» What does pebble size mean here? | *Small, like a stone you could hold | Round and shiny | Made of water | Very large, like a mountain
test: Which phrase describes a beach covered in small stones instead of sand? | A sand castle | *A pebble beach | A rocky cliff | A tide pool of water
exam: What does erosion do to rough rocks in a river, and what does the word pebble tell you about the stone that results? | Erosion makes them hot and the pebble is hot | Erosion breaks them into water so the pebble is wet | *Erosion wears them smooth, so a pebble is a small, smooth, round stone | Erosion turns them into sand, so a pebble is a grain of sand
